</b><font size="1" color="#736459">August 11. 2002 - by Njall</font><b><font size="3">&nbsp;</font></b><p align="left">Karana
down, Karana down, Karana down. Pretty much the headlines of the previous week.
We go to raid, and an hour in, the server crash - again. We truly must be
blessed to have such a fine piece of machinery to host our world! Dunno how much
VI paid to change their sales motto to: You're in our crash world now!<p align="left">However,
this didn't keep us from keeling things! The week was dedicated to Dragons
slaying, which I must say, is becoming a trademark of Darksphere! Owned ToV once
again, getting numerous armor drops to our fine members! We got it all down now,
doing it flawless each time!<p align="left">Last night we laid waste to the
Dragons of Western Wastes, picked up no less than 4 7/6 Talismans, and skinned
the cute little Tantor for his tusk. Grats to all the winners! Duppo (Tantor's
Tusk), Tonponbo, Nyriaa, Danuvil and Treelow (7/6 Talismans) Darfin (6/5
Talisman).<p align="left">In addition to all this, Darksphere challenged the
Sapara's of WW. Rak Sapara was the unlucky piece of scales, and after a flawless
pull by Gruz, we ripped it apart like it was made of paper. Drops? Dr00d and
Ranger spells... Whats made of paper, drops paper I guess.<p align="center"><a href="Kills/RakSapara.jpg" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="Kills/RakSaparasmall.jpg" width="512" height="384"></a><p align="left">&nbsp;<p align="center">&nbsp;***
